WHAT REPRODUCED, AND THE ONE THING THAT DID NOT

  ROOT (CNF)      7e6c9c26...  identical.  343,896 cubes, 0 mismatches per cube
                               AND per chunk, regenerated over 3.7 h on a compute
                               node.  DERIVED HERE, not read from the conf --
                               which is the difference between this run and the
                               previous one, and the reason gap 2 can close.
  cover_cnf       4876f077...  identical to COVER_CNF_SHA in instances/p23.conf,
                               ASSERTED by the script rather than compared by eye
                               as on 2026-09-11.
  CERT (portable) ff60539e...  identical.  It is a function of the two above and
                               both were computed in this run, so the composition
                               was RUN rather than inferred -- which is the whole
                               reason certroot.py exists.
  ROOT (proofs)   01e52ba5...  identical, which is STRONGER than section 5.2
                               promises: proof bytes are build-dependent and are
                               not required to match.
  CERT (full)     35db996f...  DIFFERS from the laptop's 0d017c74..., and that is
                               the CORRECT outcome, not a failure.  It commits to
                               LRAT bytes.  The search proofs did match, so the
                               entire difference comes from split_cover_proof
                               (55013059...), for which the conf deliberately
                               records no expectation.

COST.  08:23:59 to 13:17:37, 4 h 54 m of wall on 4 cores: root regeneration 3.7 h,
the coverage CNF written in 265 s (0.78 GiB), the solve 2,280 s with a 1,935 MiB
proof, CHECK=VERIFIED.  The cores are bought for memory, not parallelism: every
stage here is single-threaded.

THE 75 BASE VARIABLES are 5 voters x C(6,2) for the six-vertex base -- derived,
and worth stating because a stale docstring elsewhere in this project once said
50, which is the five-vertex figure.
